	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB">
			<h3 class="MainH">&nbsp;<a name="pwd">I</a> forgot my user name and/or password</h3>
		</td>
	</tr>	
	
	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB">
			<b>Not a problem. The easiest way to get it is to go to the <a class="BaseC" href="LoginHelp.asp" target="_self"><b>Login Help</b></a> page
			and simply input your email address, and the information will be sent to you. NOTE: the email address must match the one you have listed in the guild
			database, or you will not receive it. If you have any problems getting your user name/password, or can't remember which email address you are
			using, just send an email to me, <a class="BaseC" href="mailto:darren_cameron@yahoo.com"><b>Morpeth</b></a>, and I'll get to it you.</b>&nbsp;[<a class="BaseC" href="#topics">Back to top</a>]</a><p>&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB">
			<h3 class="MainH">&nbsp;<a name="acct">How</a> do I get an account?</h3>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB">
			<b>Accounts are only given to Guild members. Assuming you are one, there's a few pieces of information needed to get
			you set up; your first and last name, email address, a user name, and password. You can change your user name, password,
			and email address any time after the account has been set up.<p>
			Since we are a cross-virtuality guild, you <i>do not</i> need to be playing DAoC&copy; to have an account. If you are say
			an Armiger from EverQuest&copy;, you are more than happy to have an account on this site as well.</b><p> Email <a class="BaseC" href="mailto:darren_cameron@yahoo.com"><b>Morpeth</b></a> the required information.</b>&nbsp;[<a class="BaseC" href="#topics">Back to top</a>]<p>&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>	
	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB">
			<h3 class="MainH">&nbsp;<a name="pics1">How</a> do I upload my character's image on his/her page?</h3>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB">
			<b>While I wish Armigers could upload their own characters pics, the web hosting company we use doesn't allow for me
			to install the kind of third-party controls that are available to allow this. So unfortunately I need to do it for you. DAoC&copy; screenshots
			are usually stored in the Mythic/Camelot folder on your PC as .tga files named something like "sshot000.tga" . Those are BIG files, so they need to converted to a .gif or .jpg
			format, either by you or me. And please crop or resize your pics to something reasonable, fullsize images will be cut down to size as needed.
			If you don't have a graphics editor I can do the cropping and conversions for you.</b>
			<p>
			Email <a class="BaseC" href="mailto:darren_cameron@yahoo.com"><b>Morpeth</b></a> your pics to have them uploaded for you.&nbsp;[<a class="BaseC" href="#topics">Back to top</a>]<p>&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>	

	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB">
			<h3 class="MainH">&nbsp;<a name="pics2">Can</a> I have more than one characer pic?</h3>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB">
			<b>Yes. While the character details pages will only display one picture at a given time, I can store more than one for you. Under the character updates
			screen there is an "Image" field on the form. It should match the name of the image file you want to display.<p>
			So if you have 3 pics stored on the server, say 'Morpeth1.jpg', 'Morpeth2.jpg' and 'Morpeth3.jpg', you could change your character pic occassionally
			by changing the "Image" field value to one of those 3 file names.</b>&nbsp;[<a class="BaseC" href="#topics">Back to top</a>]</a><p>&nbsp;
		</td>
	</tr>

	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB">
			<h3 class="MainH">&nbsp;<a name="help">Do</a> you need any help with the website?</h3>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td Class="MainB">
			<b>I'm a programmer not a graphic designer, so visually the site could probably use some sprucing up. 
			If anyone likes to do graphics and has some ideas, please by all means, go for it. And of course, if you have
			ideas for new content or functionality, let me know.<p>
			As far as the actual programming goes, I can maintain the site ok on my own, but what would really
			help if is people kept their characters updated and contribute to things like the DAoC&copy; <a href="linksview.asp" class="BaseC" target="_self">links page.</a></b>&nbsp;[<a class="BaseC" href="#topics">Back to top</a>]
		</td>
	</tr>

